<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93442" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαῦλος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, an Adj. descriptive of gait and
		carriage, defined as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φαῦλον καὶ
		διερρυηκός</span> by Sch.<i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>V.</u>
			1169
		</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαῦλα ποσὶν βαίνουσα</span>,
		applied to the gait of the tortoise, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>straddling, waddling,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				h.Merc.
				28
			</span></i>; of the <i>loose, wanton</i> gait of courtesans or
			Bacchantes, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. βαίνειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anacr.
					168
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαῦλαι Βασσαρίδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					55
				</span></i>
			; also of a <i>prancing</i> horse, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. βαίνειν, ἵππος ὡς κορωνίης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Semon.
					18
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
